## Why This Is Asked

Tests around feature flags in critical flows like checkout are common in large apps. This question probes how to manage multiple UI branches, data isolation per tenant, and end-to-end integrity, including idempotency and analytics reconciliation.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flags and environment isolation
- Deterministic testing with mocks and fake timers
- Idempotent purchases and event reconciliation
- Analytics/instrumentation validation across retries

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright test skeleton for flag-gated checkout
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test.describe('Flag-gated checkout', () => {
  test('flag ON renders new UI and processes purchase', async ({ page }) => {
    // mock flag service to ON for tenant A
    await page.route('**/flags/**', route =>
      route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ flag: 'on' }) })
    );
    // proceed with purchase flow, using idempotent key
    // assert UI contains new checkout and purchase succeeds
  });

  test('flag OFF renders legacy UI and processes same purchase', async ({ page }) => {
    // mock flag service to OFF for tenant A
    await page.route('**/flags/**', route =>
      route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ flag: 'off' }) })
    );
    // proceed with same purchase flow, ensure success and analytics
  });
});
```

